{# Accomplishment / after-travel report (checklist code AR-01).

   Unlike IOT-45 and DV-32 this has no GAM appendix number — it is the narrative
   the traveller owes after the trip, and the system can only pre-fill the facts
   it already holds. The purpose text and the itinerary become the skeleton; the
   traveller signs it as their report.

   The honest limitation is stated on the page rather than hidden: the system
   knows where someone went and why they were authorised to go, not what they
   accomplished. Printing a confident-looking narrative the traveller never
   wrote would be worse than an explicit prompt to add one. #}
{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="field-grid">
  <span class="field-label">Name</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.full_name }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Position</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.position_title or "—" }}</span>

  <span class="field-label">Division</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.division or "—" }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Travel order</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claim.dpo_no or "—" }}</span>

  <span class="field-label">Destination</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claim.destination or "—" }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Inclusive dates</span>
  <span class="field-value">
    {{ claim.date_depart | manila_date }} – {{ claim.date_return | manila_date }}
  </span>
</div>

<h2>Authorised purpose</h2>
<p>{{ claim.purpose or "—" }}</p>

<h2>Places visited</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Date</th>
      <th>Place</th>
      <th>Means of transport</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for leg in legs %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ leg.leg_date | manila_date }}</td>
      <td>{{ leg.place or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ leg.transport_mode or "—" }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="3">No itinerary legs recorded.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Accomplishments and observations</h2>
<p class="note">
  To be completed by the traveller before signing. The system pre-fills the
  authorised purpose and the itinerary above; the narrative below is yours.
</p>
<div class="signature-line" style="height: 28mm; border-bottom: none;
     border: 0.5pt solid var(--oc-color-border);"></div>

<div class="signature-row">
  <div class="signature-block">
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-name">{{ claimant.full_name }}</p>
    <p class="signature-role">Traveller — report submitted</p>
  </div>
  <div class="signature-block">
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-name">&nbsp;</p>
    <p class="signature-role">Noted — immediate supervisor</p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
